# AWS IAM Security Lab

## Objective

Configure a secure AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) administration lab using group-based access and multi-factor authentication (MFA).

## Lab Activities Completed

- Secured the AWS root account with MFA.
- Created a `Lab-Administrators` IAM group.
- Attached the AWS-managed `AdministratorAccess` policy to the lab group for controlled administrative practice.
- Created a `lab-admin` IAM user.
- Assigned the `lab-admin` user to the `Lab-Administrators` group instead of assigning permissions directly to the user.
- Protected the `lab-admin` user with MFA.

## IAM Concepts Demonstrated

- User provisioning
- Authentication and MFA
- Authorization
- Role-based and group-based access control
- User account administration
- Security controls
- Enterprise IAM fundamentals

## Security Note

This is a personal AWS lab environment. No production data, passwords, access keys, secret keys, recovery codes, or AWS account identifiers are included in this repository.
